# Commit-identity normalization for `git log` / `git shortlog`.
#
# One identity per contributor. The ralph loop wrote most of this repository
# under several spellings of the same bot; they collapse here so the history
# reads as three authors instead of twelve. The canonical human address is the
# one that actually receives mail - the catbee.ca spellings were never
# provisioned. The agent identities stay separate on purpose: a person signs
# the boundary, but the machine-authored commits stay labelled as such (see
# docs/ai-contribution-stance.md).
#
# This is display only. No commit is rewritten, so a BUILD_ID quoted by an
# installed image still resolves to a real commit in this history.

